  "prefLabel": "Par 203.02 Scheduling",
  "priorExpiration": "2008-07-09",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Par 203.02 Scheduling. All inmates shall receive a parole hearing within the 60-day period prior to their minimum parole date. If parole is denied at the initial hearing, the board shall advise the inmate, in writing via a copy of the minutes of the hearing, what the inmate shall be required to do to be granted another hearing.\n\nSource. #7149, eff 12-7-99, EXPIRED: 12-7-07\n\nNew. #9070, INTERIM, eff 1-11-08, EXPIRED: 7-9-08\n\nNew. #9254, eff 9-6-08; ss by #12157, eff 4-7-17",
